{"archetypes":[{"name":"state-propagation","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The Gate B mode determination has a novel dual-read (in-memory manual_requested OR disk manual_gate_b) that must survive Bash subshell boundaries; the four-arm recovery in SKILL.md is the only guard for the write-failure path, but normal runs depend entirely on run-params.json being readable at Gate B time.","prompt_body":"Examine the Gate B mode determination logic in `skills/design/references/approval-gates.md` (the 'Gate B mode (auto-apply vs manual)' subsection) and verify whether the claim 'if the in-memory boolean `manual_requested` from Step 0b is still bound' is achievable across Bash subshell boundaries — Gate B fires in a separate subshell from Step 0b, so argv-parsed variables will not be present without explicit export or disk persistence. Verify that the four-arm recovery block in `skills/design/SKILL.md` Step 0b (outer `if`, jq merge filter, elif warning, graceful-degrade fallback) only fires on write-failure, meaning normal successful runs depend entirely on `jq -r '.manual_gate_b // false'` against a readable `run-params.json` at every Gate B re-entry — check whether the Step 3 re-entry from Gate C(c) and the brainstorm ad-hoc Q&A path in Step 0b sub-step 4 guarantee `run-params.json` is already written and contains `manual_gate_b` before Gate B is reached. Also check whether the elif jq-unavailable warning branch in SKILL.md Step 0b prints a warning but fails to persist `manual_gate_b` to disk, meaning a `--manual`-only run where jq is absent would silently auto-apply despite the operator's intent. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"behavioral-compat","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"The default flip from 'always prompt at Gate B' to 'auto-apply' is a breaking UX change for existing operators; every code path through /design that reaches Gate B must correctly propagate manual_gate_b, including the already-planned ad-hoc Q&A branch and the Pre-Step-0 brainstorm upgrade flow.","prompt_body":"Audit every code path through `skills/design/SKILL.md` that reaches Step 3.5 Gate B and confirm `manual_gate_b` is correctly read and honored on each path, paying special attention to the Step 0b sub-step 4 'already-planned branch' ad-hoc Q&A path (where `brainstorm_requested=true` triggers Step 1d.5 then exits — does `manual_requested` get written to `run-params.json` before that exit if the operator also passed `--manual`?). Verify the Pre-Step-0 brainstorm upgrade path (where `--trivial` + `--brainstorm` becomes effective `--simple`) correctly preserves `manual_requested` through the tier remap so `write-run-params.sh` receives `--manual-gate-b true` even after the upgrade. Check whether the SKILL.md Pre-Step-0 mutual-exclusion block introduces any implicit exclusion of `--manual` with any other flag (the plan says it is independent, but the diff must be checked for accidental gate collisions). Also confirm that the new default auto-apply behavior is visible to operators before they invoke `/design` — check whether `README.md`, `docs/skills.md`, and `docs/workflow-lifecycle.md` updates are prominent enough to prevent silent plan modification for operators who have not read the changelog. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"apply-body-consistency","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The core structural change factors the Apply-all body into a named subsection referenced from two call sites; if the extracted body omits any step or if the count-based test-design-structure.sh pin is fooled by the subsection heading itself, the no-copy-paste guarantee breaks silently.","prompt_body":"Examine the `### Apply-all body` subsection in `skills/design/references/approval-gates.md` and compare its steps against the prior inline Apply-all option (a) body — verify the dedup-sweep prose, `ACTION=EMIT_PLAN` re-emit, `invoke-plan-validator-if-not-quick.sh` invocation, and Step 2b.5 call are all present and in the original order with no prose truncation. Verify that both call sites — the auto-apply branch and the manual Apply-all option (a) — use the identical reference phrase `Execute \`### Apply-all body\` verbatim`, and check whether the `test-design-structure.sh` pin `apply_all_reference_count >= 2` (using `grep -Fc`) could be satisfied by the subsection heading line itself (`### Apply-all body`) rather than the two genuine call-site references, inflating the count and masking a missing reference. Also examine whether the 'Go through each' per-finding iteration path's inline dedup-sweep prose in `approval-gates.md` now silently diverges from the `### Apply-all body` dedup-sweep, since it intentionally cannot reuse the subsection (it applies a subset), and whether that divergence surface is documented or pinned in the test harness. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
